# BKP-59: Import leaves auto backup cancelled until a real process startup
# reschedules it.
#
# The import's own restart must be suppressed in phase one because it calls
# exit(0) in the instrumentation process, which cannot report a successful test
# result afterward. The host-driven boundary then starts a second instrumentation
# process. Creating that process runs the production App.onCreate before phase
# two can inspect WorkManager; the test never calls AutoBackupScheduler itself.
describe Imported auto backup is rescheduled by a real process startup

# Imports autoBackupEnabled=true with no backup folder, verifies the pipeline's
# terminal cancellation left no live work, and commits the preference to disk.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.backup.AutoBackupProcessRestartTest#phaseOneImportAutoBackupOnAndLeaveTheScheduleCancelled

kill-app

# Starting this instrumentation phase creates the application and executes the
# real App.onCreate. The phase asserts that startup enqueued the worker, then
# proves the no-folder run records a visible failure.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.backup.AutoBackupProcessRestartTest#phaseTwoAssertProcessStartupRescheduledTheImportedPreference
